<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hats (party)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1730s–<a href="/years/1772">1772</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Hat party</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hats were one of the two political parties of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/age-of-liberty">Age of Liberty</a>, dominated by the nobility and officers and in power from 1738 to 1765. They favoured mercantilist economic policies and an alliance with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> aimed at reversing Swedish losses to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, which led to the disastrous war of 1741–1743 and to participation in the Seven Years' War. Their rivals were the Caps.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>After Charles XII’s death the Age of Liberty (1719–1772) gave power to the Riksdag and its parties, the <b>Hats</b> and the Caps, until Gustav III’s coup of 1772.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-sweden">Kingdom of Sweden · Governance &amp; Law</a></li></ul></section>
